<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Two learners push a loaded handcart (mkokoteni) across a flat yard. Seen from above, with east and north positive, their pushes are <m>\mathbf{F}_1 = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 70 \\ -30 \end{array}\right)}</m> N and <m>\mathbf{F}_2 = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -30 \\ 60 \end{array}\right)}</m> N.</p><p>(a) Write the resultant force <m>\mathbf{F}_1 + \mathbf{F}_2</m>.</p><div><m>\mathbf{F}_1 + \mathbf{F}_2 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/> N  </div><p>(b) Find the size of the resultant force, exact or to 2 decimal places.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> N  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Add the east parts and add the north parts: <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 70 \\ -30 \end{array}\right)} + {\left(\begin{array}{c} -30 \\ 60 \end{array}\right)} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 40 \\ 30 \end{array}\right)}</m> N.</p><p>(b) <m>|\mathbf{R}| = \sqrt{({40})^2 + ({30})^2} = \sqrt{{2500}}</m> <m>= {50}</m> N.</p><p>The sizes of the two pushes add up to <m>{143.24}</m> N, more than <m>|\mathbf{R}|</m>: the learners push in different directions, so part of each push is wasted.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 40 \\ 30 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>50</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>